{"id": "EUVD-2026-107016", "enisaUuid": "9f5b88f8-6468-30b7-94bc-859b8f234c81", "description": "Trigger.dev before 4.7.3 contains a tenant filtering bypass vulnerability that allows authenticated users to read other tenants' data by using placeholder table syntax in POST /api/v1/query. Attackers can submit queries with FROM {database.table} expressions, including within subqueries, to skip table allowlist and tenant filters and expose run metadata and payloads.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T00:36:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T15:50:31", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/triggerdotdev/trigger.dev/security/advisories/GHSA-m79r-84cc-xwg9", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/trigger-dev-before-4.7.3-tenant-filtering-bypass-via-query-table-placeholders"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-114065", "GHSA-hgfc-cgqx-gchc"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.3, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1bb85300-6aec-32cb-ba81-0f30d097bf67", "product": {"name": "trigger.dev", "vendor": {"name": "triggerdotdev"}}, "product_version": "0 <4.7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5538916e-92cb-3cd4-bdec-be85b8d981ed", "vendor": {"name": "triggerdotdev"}}], "isExploited": false}